From e97cb316e73fba0964e39ccdf82c978fe99a7adc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:11:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the sparse solvers of MAGMA

When MFEM is built with MAGMA in double precision, and the library of the
sparse part of MAGMA (magma_sparse) and its header are found next to the
library of MAGMA used by MFEM (or given by MFEM_MGIS_MAGMA_SPARSE_LIBRARY
and MFEM_MGIS_MAGMA_SPARSE_INCLUDE_DIR), the module of MAGMA registers:
- the Krylov solvers MAGMACG, MAGMABiCGSTAB, MAGMAGMRES (restarted
  flexible GMRES, option KDim), MAGMAIDR (option ShadowSpaceDimension),
  MAGMACGS, MAGMAQMR and MAGMATFQMR, in sequential, which only accept the
  preconditioners of MAGMA and apply them themselves;
- the preconditioners MAGMAJacobi, MAGMAILU and MAGMAIC (incomplete LU
  and Cholesky factorizations without fill-in of cuSPARSE or hipSPARSE),
  given to any solver, and applied to the diagonal block of each process
  in parallel.

They compute on one GPU (an error is reported without GPU: MAGMA is
initialized without one). The matrix is copied on the host, its columns
being sorted, then on the GPU for each operator. The vectors of MFEM are
given to MAGMA when MFEM computes on the GPU, the device being
synchronized before (the queue of MAGMA does not wait for the kernels of
MFEM), and copied in vectors kept between the resolutions otherwise. The
solvers are called directly, with the defaults of MAGMA set by mfem-mgis:
magma_dparse_opts prints its usage on each call.

Defects of MAGMA 2.10 handled:
- the preconditioned TFQMR reports its breakdowns as successes: a
  resolution is reported as converged only if the residual recomputed by
  MAGMA at the end is lower than ten times the tolerance;
- the transposed incomplete Cholesky factorization, used by QMR, applies
  its factors in the wrong order: QMR refuses this preconditioner (the
  incomplete LU factorization is the same for a symmetric matrix);
- the Jacobi preconditioner only detects a missing diagonal entry, the
  incomplete factorizations nothing: a null or missing diagonal entry is
  refused, on all the processes in parallel;
- with a null right hand side and an initial guess, the residuals relative
  to the right hand side are not defined: the solution is set to zero.
The module is exported to the installed configuration
(MFEMMGIS_HAVE_MAGMA_SPARSE).
